%I A401244 #23 Nov 11 2026 10:11:33
%S A401244 77017,77041,50592937,50616073,50616121,50616143,50616359,50616617,
%T A401244 50616619,50616847,50616869,50616877,50616967,50616971,50617013,
%U A401244 50617019,50617169,50617201,50620223,50620243,50620307,50620487,50620499,50620673,50620753,50620763,50620771
%N A401244 Primes p for which pi_{24;7,17}(p) - pi_{24;1,23}(p) = -1, where pi_{m;a,b,...}(x) is the number of primes <= x which are congruent to a or b or ... (mod m).
%C A401244 From _Leandro Hector Gallego_ and _Jianing Song_: (Start)
%C A401244 This sequence is about one of the 21 prime races modulo 24 between cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see A401958 for more details. Specifically, here we have H = {1,23} and S = {7,17}, corresponding to T = {chi_12, chi_24}, where chi_d = (d/.) is the Kronecker symbol viewed as a character modulo N = 24.
%C A401244 This sequence gives primes p such that Sum_{primes q<=p} (chi_12(q) + chi_24(q))/2 = 1.
%C A401244 Assuming GRH and LI (see A401958), the set of x with pi_{24;7,17}(x) > pi_{24;1,23}(x) has logarithmic density 0.98489, making the race between {1,23} and {7,17} the 16th most biased among the 21 races of cosets of index 4 in (Z/24Z)*; see the Zenodo preprint below.
%C A401244 Let D(x) = pi_{24;7,17}(x) - pi_{24;1,23}(x). Below x0 = 7*10^12 there are respectively 30659637567, 30659688364, 30659698140, 30659716342, 30659718072, 30659718286, 30659752652, and 30659759379 primes congruent to 1, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, or 23 modulo 24, giving D(x0) = 19480. There are 5 sign-changing zones giving a total of 11447 terms below x0:
%C A401244   (1) a(1..2) = 77017-77041;
%C A401244   (2) a(3..288) = 50592937-50979847 (there are 7672 primes a(3) <= p <= a(288) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -74 at p = 50774519);
%C A401244   (3) a(289..3604) = 4643545703-4801209113 (there are 1688558 primes a(289) <= p <= a(3604) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -768 at p = 4780884023);
%C A401244   (4) a(3605..11426) = 5132617753-5257799611 (there are 966186 primes a(3605) <= p <= a(11426) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -330 at p = 5150305871);
%C A401244   (5) a(11427..11447) = 82458129503-82458130687 (there are 42 primes a(11427) <= p <= a(11447) such that D(p) < 0, with D(p) reaching a minimum of -4 at p = 82458130537).
%C A401244 The total number of primes p <= x0 with D(p) < 0 is 2662460. (End)
%H A401244 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="/A401244/b401244.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..11447</a> (all terms below 7*10^12; a(1)-a(11426) from Jianing Song, a(11427)-a(11440) corrected by Leandro Hector Gallego)
%H A401244 Leandro Hector Gallego, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.24020025">Logarithmic densities of prime number races between the cosets of a subgroup of index 4 modulo 24</a>, preprint, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A401244 Greg Martin and Daniel Fiorilli, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Chennai-31Aug10.pdf">Prime number races: An asymptotic formula for the densities</a>, Analytic and Combinatorial Number Theory, Institute of Mathematical Sciences, Chennai, India. August 31, 2010.
%H A401244 Greg Martin, <a href="https://personal.math.ubc.ca/~gerg/slides/Canberra-29Nov18.pdf">Prime number races</a>, Pure Math Seminar, UNSW Canberra. November 29, 2018.
%H A401244 Andrey S. Shchebetov, <a href="https://math101.guru/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/01-A3-Presentation-v7.3EN-no.pdf">Testing Chebyshev's bias for prime numbers up to 10^15</a>, EUCYS 2018.
%H A401244 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chebyshev%27s_bias">Chebyshev's bias</a>.
%o A401244 (PARI) my(k=0); forprime(p=2, 1e11, if(p%24==1||p%24==23, k--); if(p%24==7||p%24==17, k++); if(k==-1, print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A401244 See A401958 for related sequences.
%K A401244 nonn,changed
%O A401244 1,1
%A A401244 _Jianing Song_, Oct 18 2026
